# Documentation (Doxygen → HTML and PDF)

All documentation is generated with Doxygen from the repository `Doxyfile` (`scripts/docs.ps1`). HTML goes to `out/docs/html`; LaTeX goes to `out/docs/latex`, where `make.bat` builds `refman.pdf`. Docs must build offline with **zero warnings** for code you touched.

## What must be documented

- Every header: a file comment with `@file`, `@brief`, and `@req` for the requirements it implements.
- Every public or protected class, struct, enum, enumerator, function, method, type alias, concept and data member.
- Every function: `@brief`, each `@param` (with direction `[in]`, `[out]` or `[in,out]` where not obvious), `@return`, and `@units` for physical quantities. Use `@pre`, `@post`, `@note`, `@warning` and `@see` where they add information.
- Commands exposed on the command bus: `@cmd` with the command name.
- Private implementation: brief `//` comments explaining *why*, not *what*.

## Comment style

Use `///` line comments for Doxygen blocks. Put declarations' docs in headers, not in `.cpp` files.

```cpp
// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The APP Authors

/// @file   SketchSolver.h
/// @brief  Geometric constraint solver for 2D sketches.
/// @req    M-SKT-02

#pragma once

#include "core/Result.h"
#include "sketch/Sketch.h"

namespace app::sketch
{

/// @brief Options that control a sketch solve.
struct SolveOptions
{
    int    maxIterations = 50;    ///< Upper bound on Newton iterations.
    double tolerance     = 1e-10; ///< Residual norm treated as solved. @units mm
};

/// @brief Solves the constraint system of a sketch in place.
///
/// Uses damped Newton iterations with degree-of-freedom analysis. On failure the
/// sketch geometry is left unchanged.
///
/// @req M-SKT-02
class SketchSolver
{
public:
    /// @brief  Solve every constraint in @p sketch.
    /// @param[in,out] sketch   Sketch to solve; entity parameters are updated on success.
    /// @param[in]     options  Iteration limit and tolerance.
    /// @return Solve status, or an error if the constraint system is inconsistent.
    /// @cmd    sketch.solve
    [[nodiscard]] Result<SolveStatus> solve( Sketch& sketch, const SolveOptions& options );
};

} // namespace app::sketch
```

## Markdown documentation

- Narrative docs live in `docs/` as Markdown and are included in the Doxygen build (`docs/mainpage.md` is the main page). Give every page a level-1 heading and an `{#page-id}` anchor so it can be cross-referenced: `# File format {#format}`.
- Each module has `src/<module>/README.md` (purpose, allowed dependencies, main types). Doxygen picks it up as a module page.
- File-format docs (`docs/format/`) are the public, normative specification of the file format. Keep them in sync with the JSON Schemas in the same change.
- Diagrams: prefer Doxygen `@dot` blocks or committed SVG/PNG under `docs/images/`. No externally hosted images.
- The `@req` alias builds a "Requirements Traceability" page automatically. Tag implementing classes and functions with the requirement IDs they satisfy.
